{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "id": "apc-40-mk2-default-1",
  "name": "APC40 mkII Default (Playback)",
  "status": "community",
  "notes": "Default for the AKAI APC40 mkII (Generic Mode). Faders -> executors 201-208 (+ master 209, crossfader 210). Top Track-Control knobs -> executor faders 401-408; Device-Control encoders -> 411-418 (only transmit while Track 1 is the selected device bank). 5x8 RGB clip grid (PAD 1 = top-left) -> executor Keys, top->bottom 341-348 / 331-338 / 321-328 / 311-318 / 301-308, with PAM-10 rgb-color feedback: each pad reflects its executor's live MA3 sequence colour (nearest palette entry), lit while running. Clip Stop mirrors each track fader (201-208); Activator/Solo/Record Arm -> 221-228 / 231-238 / 241-248. Section buttons Device On/Off/Lock, Clip/Device View, Detail View -> executor Keys 251-254; the 4 arrows -> Up/Down (Device) + Prev/Next (Bank). Scene Launch (RGB) = Go/Pause/Go Back/Off/Highlight; Stop All = Escape. Transport: Play=Go, Record=Store, Session=Update, Shift=MA key, Bank=Clear, Up/Down=Page Up/Down, Nudge +/- = Go Fast/Back Fast. Cue Level (signed relative encoder) nudges executor 211. UNMAPPED: Tempo, Track Select/Master (no MIDI in Generic Mode), Crossfader-A|B row, Pan/Sends/User/Metronome/Tap Tempo, transport Left/Right. status=community: NOT yet verified on hardware.",
  "deviceDefinitionId": "apc-40-mk2",
